    {
      "id": "far-cf-start-and-revenue-q-e00d7729",
      "type": "long",
      "stem": "Analyse the first three Circle Films transactions on the accounting equation and show the totals after each.",
      "options": [],
      "answer": "",
      "accept": [],
      "explanation": "",
      "model_answer_md": "**Transaction 1: shares issued for ₹15,000 cash.** Cash +₹15,000; Common Stock +₹15,000. Assets ₹15,000 = Liabilities ₹0 + Equity ₹15,000.\n\n**Transaction 2: camera ₹9,000 and memory cards ₹1,000.** Cash -₹10,000 (to ₹5,000); Supplies +₹1,000; Equipment +₹9,000. An exchange of assets, so total assets stay ₹15,000 = ₹0 + ₹15,000.\n\n**Transaction 3: ₹1,500 received for filming a wedding.** Cash +₹1,500 (to ₹6,500). The inflow from a service is revenue, so Retained Earnings +₹1,500. Assets ₹16,500 = Liabilities ₹0 + Equity ₹16,500 (common stock ₹15,000 + retained earnings ₹1,500).\n\nThe equation balances after each transaction.",
      "rubric": [
        {
          "point": "Transaction 1 with totals",
          "source_ref": "far--practice-circle-films-transaction-analysis#1"
        },
        {
          "point": "Transaction 2 as an exchange of assets",
          "source_ref": "far--practice-circle-films-transaction-analysis#1"
        },
        {
          "point": "Transaction 3 as revenue",
          "source_ref": "far--practice-circle-films-transaction-analysis#1"
        },
        {
          "point": "Totals 15,000, 15,000 and 16,500",
          "source_ref": "far--practice-circle-films-transaction-analysis#1"
        },
        {
          "point": "Equation balances each time",
          "source_ref": "far--practice-circle-films-transaction-analysis#1"
        }
      ],
      "marks": 8.0,
